    "number": 242,
    "title": "feat(#122): implement linear_scan_in_loop lint",
    "body": "## Description\n\nImplements a new lint \\linear_scan_in_loop\\ that detects linear-scan methods (\\contains\\, \\position\\, \\\find\\) on Soroban collection types (\\Vec\\, \\Map\\) inside a loop body, where the scanned collection is not the collection being iterated.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nA \\Vec::contains\\ or \\iter().position()\\ inside a loop turns O(n) into O(n²). In Soroban every element access on a host-side collection is a metered host call, so the quadratic term is paid in real instructions. This is the most common way a contract that tests fine on 10 elements becomes unaffordable on 1000.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Matches method calls on \\soroban_sdk::vec::Vec\\ and \\soroban_sdk::map::Map\\ types.\n- Reuses existing \\enclosing_loop()\\ and \\depends_on_loop_state()\\ helpers.\n- Only flags when the scanned collection does NOT depend on loop state (i.e., it's the same collection every iteration), avoiding false positives when iterating the collection itself.\n\n## Known false positives\n\n- A collection scanned inside a closure body nested in the loop is still flagged (existing limitation of \\depends_on_loop_state\\)\n- Collection-like wrappers not matching the exact type path are missed (conservative by design)\n\n## Changes\n\n| File | Action |\n|------|--------|\n| \\soroban_cost_lints/src/lib.rs\\ | Added \\LINEAR_SCAN_IN_LOOP\\ lint, \\LinearScanInLoop\\ pass, \\LINT_METADATA\\ entry, pass registration |\n| \\soroban_cost_lints/ui/main.rs\\ | Added \\Vec\\/\\Map\\ stubs, 4 test fixtures |\n| \\docs/lints/linear_scan_in_loop.md\\ | Created per-lint documentation page |\n\nCloses #122",
